# Add this line to the droplet's existing crontab (crontab -e) alongside
# the tri-cities-7day-forecast and western-us-noaa-outlooks lines already
# there. Needs the same WB_API_KEY already exported at the top of that
# crontab (WindBorne account/key, shared across every project that uses it
# -- no new key needed here).
#
# WM-6 updates hourly, so this runs hourly too, 10 min past the hour as a
# starting buffer -- unlike the SPC/IEM buffer in western-us-noaa-outlooks,
# this hasn't been empirically checked against a live cycle boundary yet.
# Worth confirming against a few real days of state/publish.log (does the
# forecast's own "init" timestamp actually advance every single run, or
# does it sometimes still show the previous hour's cycle?) and tightening
# or loosening this if it's off.
#
# Before the first run: seed each location's climatology cache once --
#   cd /opt/ingalls-weather-scripts/850-700-temp-chart
#   venv/bin/python3 deploy/seed_climatology.py
# publish_charts.py will hard-fail any location whose cached climatology
# file is missing, rather than silently skipping the climatology overlay.

10 * * * * /opt/ingalls-weather-scripts/850-700-temp-chart/venv/bin/python3 /opt/ingalls-weather-scripts/850-700-temp-chart/deploy/publish_charts.py >> /opt/ingalls-weather-scripts/850-700-temp-chart/state/cron.log 2>&1
